.983666,"area":609},{"id":715,"colour":76,"x":0.671419,"y":0.983943,"area":576},{"id":716,"colour":3,"x":0.919721,"y":0.984903,"area":523},{"id":717,"colour":77,"x":0.343379,"y":0.986479,"area":562}],"source":{"title":"Butterflies are my new interest and if I see something interest, am happy to spend time to get some good shots. This is a Blue tiger, similar to its other cousin, the common tiger. I chased it for a short distance trying to get a good shot and grabbed a few shots while on this flower. Only later during review in the laptop did I see the little fly on the bird and they seemed to share the sweetness of the flower! What a lovely surprise! Did you know that most butterflies are poisonous to birds? There are some that are not, but many are. The few that are not, mimic the poisonous ones - a form of mimicry called the Batesian Mimicry. It is an interested read! Thanks in advance for your views and / or feedback. Much appreciated.","creator":"Hari K Patibanda","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","pageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/?curid=110193325","provider":"Wikimedia Commons"}}